{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786254356401,"sessionID":"ses_01b038435ffe8s23kM0wHD2vvA","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_00_ET_YSfwOUydbQVLWBbqbNoS2829","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md","oldString":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [ ] Q1: Which specific non-DeepSeek providers in `.pi/settings.json` (minimax/MiniMax-M3, xiaomi/mimo-v2.5-pro, xiaomi/mimo-v2.5-pro-ultraspeed, opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free, opencode-go/qwen3.8-max, opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash, openai-codex/gpt-5.6-*) receive which cache-optimization treatment, and is each correct?\n- [ ] Q2: Does the guard actually leave the surface exclusively non-DeepSeek, given `isDeepPiOwned` is provider-scoped to `deepseek/` while deepseek-class model ids exist under opencode/opencode-go providers?\n- [ ] Q3: Are the per-provider adapter classifications (Kimi/Qwen/GLM/MiniMax/Mimo/Hunyuan/Mistral/Grok/Llama) correct and complete, and what does each actually do beyond the generic OpenAI normalizer?\n- [ ] Q4: What are the cache-hit-rate economics levers for official OpenAI and third-party OpenAI-compatible endpoints (prompt_cache_key, prompt_cache_retention gating, prompt rewrite bypass for responses-family)?\n- [ ] Q5: Is the Anthropic TTL-reordering repair path correct for all Anthropic-like models (incl. OpenAI-compatible Claude proxies with cacheControlFormat: \"anthropic\")?\n- [ ] Q6: Are the raw usage normalizers (OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini) correct for each provider's real usage shape, and where do cacheWrite/cacheRead accounting gaps exist?\n- [ ] Q7: How wide is the test suite's provider coverage, and which non-DeepSeek provider paths are untested?\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->","newString":"<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n\n- [x] Q1: Which specific non-DeepSeek providers in `.pi/settings.json` receive which cache-optimization treatment, and is each correct? (answered: coverage matrix in research.md §5)\n- [x] Q2: Does the guard actually leave the surface exclusively non-DeepSeek? (answered: NO — two enabled DeepSeek-class models remain active surface; isDeepPiOwned is provider-scoped)\n- [x] Q3: Are the per-provider adapter classifications correct and complete? (answered: classification exists for all; all are thin wrappers over the generic OpenAI normalizer; Gemini normalizer mismatch on openai-completions transport)\n- [x] Q4: What are the cache-hit-rate economics levers? (answered: zero contribution to codex workload; prompt_cache_key has no self-heal; retention strip is best-guarded; rewrite unverified for third-party)\n- [x] Q5: Is the Anthropic TTL-reordering repair correct for all Anthropic-like models? (answered: unreachable for cacheControlFormat:anthropic endpoints; over-broad downgrade; brittle error matcher)\n- [x] Q6: Are the raw usage normalizers correct? (answered: denominators consistent full-prompt; Anthropic/Gemini full misses drop out on foreign-provider path; cacheWrite display Anthropic-only)\n- [x] Q7: How wide is the test suite's provider coverage? (answered: entire non-DeepSeek provider-specific surface untested)\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -33,15 +33,15 @@\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n \n-- [ ] Q1: Which specific non-DeepSeek providers in `.pi/settings.json` (minimax/MiniMax-M3, xiaomi/mimo-v2.5-pro, xiaomi/mimo-v2.5-pro-ultraspeed, opencode/deepseek-v4-flash-free, opencode-go/qwen3.8-max, opencode-go/deepseek-v4-flash, openai-codex/gpt-5.6-*) receive which cache-optimization treatment, and is each correct?\n-- [ ] Q2: Does the guard actually leave the surface exclusively non-DeepSeek, given `isDeepPiOwned` is provider-scoped to `deepseek/` while deepseek-class model ids exist under opencode/opencode-go providers?\n-- [ ] Q3: Are the per-provider adapter classifications (Kimi/Qwen/GLM/MiniMax/Mimo/Hunyuan/Mistral/Grok/Llama) correct and complete, and what does each actually do beyond the generic OpenAI normalizer?\n-- [ ] Q4: What are the cache-hit-rate economics levers for official OpenAI and third-party OpenAI-compatible endpoints (prompt_cache_key, prompt_cache_retention gating, prompt rewrite bypass for responses-family)?\n-- [ ] Q5: Is the Anthropic TTL-reordering repair path correct for all Anthropic-like models (incl. OpenAI-compatible Claude proxies with cacheControlFormat: \"anthropic\")?\n-- [ ] Q6: Are the raw usage normalizers (OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini) correct for each provider's real usage shape, and where do cacheWrite/cacheRead accounting gaps exist?\n-- [ ] Q7: How wide is the test suite's provider coverage, and which non-DeepSeek provider paths are untested?\n+- [x] Q1: Which specific non-DeepSeek providers in `.pi/settings.json` receive which cache-optimization treatment, and is each correct? (answered: coverage matrix in research.md §5)\n+- [x] Q2: Does the guard actually leave the surface exclusively non-DeepSeek? (answered: NO — two enabled DeepSeek-class models remain active surface; isDeepPiOwned is provider-scoped)\n+- [x] Q3: Are the per-provider adapter classifications correct and complete? (answered: classification exists for all; all are thin wrappers over the generic OpenAI normalizer; Gemini normalizer mismatch on openai-completions transport)\n+- [x] Q4: What are the cache-hit-rate economics levers? (answered: zero contribution to codex workload; prompt_cache_key has no self-heal; retention strip is best-guarded; rewrite unverified for third-party)\n+- [x] Q5: Is the Anthropic TTL-reordering repair correct for all Anthropic-like models? (answered: unreachable for cacheControlFormat:anthropic endpoints; over-broad downgrade; brittle error matcher)\n+- [x] Q6: Are the raw usage normalizers correct? (answered: denominators consistent full-prompt; Anthropic/Gemini full misses drop out on foreign-provider path; cacheWrite display Anthropic-only)\n+- [x] Q7: How wide is the test suite's provider coverage? (answered: entire non-DeepSeek provider-specific surface untested)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n \n ---\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/cli-external-orchestration/039-pi-caching-like-reasonix/011-research-non-deepseek-optimization/research/lineages/deepseek-flash/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Developmen